        <h1>Clean ground first. Close access only when it is safe.</h1>
        <p class="sub">When someone has had access to your phone, accounts, or devices, the safest path is rarely the fastest one. This is a calm, private, safety-aware conversation about your digital exposure — planned around your safety, not rushed.</p>
        <div class="hero-cta">
            <a class="btn" href="#contact">If it is safe to do so, contact privately for a safety-aware conversation</a>
        </div>
        <p class="trust">In person · With you present · No remote access · No cloud processing · No retained logs</p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
        <div class="head">
            <span class="eyebrow">Safety first</span>
            <h2>If you are in immediate danger.</h2>
            <p class="lede">If you are in immediate danger, call the police at <a href="tel:100">100</a>, or Israel's national domestic-violence hotline at <a href="tel:118">118</a> — staffed 24/7 in Hebrew, Arabic, Russian, English and Amharic (you can also send a WhatsApp message to <a href="tel:050-2270118">050-2270118</a>). This page is about planning your digital safety calmly — it is not a substitute for a safety plan, an advocate, or your lawyer.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
        <div class="head">
            <span class="eyebrow">Why timing matters</span>
            <h2>A sudden change can be visible.</h2>
            <p class="lede">Changing a password, turning off location sharing, or removing a device can be visible to someone who is watching — and a sudden change can escalate the situation. Whether and when to make a change depends on your circumstances. The aim is to avoid tipping anyone off before you are ready and safe.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
        <div class="head">
            <span class="eyebrow">Clean ground first</span>
            <h2>Sometimes the safest first step is new ground.</h2>
            <p class="lede">Sometimes the safest first step is to set up new, separate ground — a device or account the other person has never had access to — rather than changing what they can already see. A safety-aware conversation can help you think this through before you act. With you, and in coordination with your safety plan or advocate where relevant, we can help you understand where you may be exposed, what is safe to change and when, and how to sequence it. Nothing is done remotely, nothing is uploaded, and no log of your digital life is kept.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
        <div class="head">
            <span class="eyebrow">What not to do abruptly</span>
            <h2>Your safety comes before speed.</h2>
            <p class="lede">Please don't rush to "close everything" at once, confront the other person with what you've found, or assume a single change makes you safe. We won't promise that any change is invisible, or that it can all be done in one day — your safety comes before speed.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
