            <h2>You don't have to do this alone.</h2>
            <p>Specialist domestic-abuse organizations, advocates, and your lawyer can help with safety planning, legal protection, and housing. We work alongside them, not in place of them.</p>
        </div>
        <ul class="cred-list">
            <li><b>National domestic-violence hotline:</b> <a href="tel:118">118</a> — confidential, 24/7, multilingual. In an emergency, police <a href="tel:100">100</a>.</li>
            <li><b>Ministry of Health — recognizing abuse and getting help:</b> <a href="https://me.health.gov.il/en/parenting/know-more/family-parental-welfare/warning-signs-of-domestic-violence/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">English</a> · <a href="https://me.health.gov.il/parenting/learn-more/family-parental-welfare/warning-signs-of-domestic-violence/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">עברית</a>.</li>
            <li><b>Red Lines (Drawing the Lines) — support &amp; resource directory:</b> <a href="https://www.redlines.org.il/en/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">English</a> · <a href="https://www.redlines.org.il/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">עברית</a>.</li>
            <li><b>If and when you're ready:</b> if it is safe to do so, you can reach out privately by WhatsApp or Signal with a short, neutral message — no details, no screenshots. We'll talk about timing and next steps at your pace.</li>
